Several of the new tests only check that a bool reaches the next layer, or repeat assertions made elsewhere. If the plumbing broke, `TestBitwiseParityQwen35DebugVarlenDirect::test_no_pinned_cpu_copy` and the direct-load engine-loop tests would already fail. Suggest deleting (about 120 lines):
- this test: heavily mocked `Generator.__init__`, only checks that kwargs are forwarded;
- `test_fetch_model_state_dict_to_gpu_reaches_model_registration` (L835): kwarg forwarding;
- `test_load_model_state_dict_direct_fetches_into_the_model` (L547): a one-line forward plus `_maybe_reset_kv_cache`, which the existing reset test already covers;
- `test_prefetch_model_state_dict_is_noop_with_fetch_to_gpu` (L614): `test_direct_load_reads_torchstore_on_the_actor_loop_during_the_load` already asserts `reads == []` after prefetch;
- `test_direct_load_groups_rejects_unsharded_params` (`test_vllm_wrapper.py:483`): tests an internal `assert`.

